  narrator: 0
  playerThoughts: 0
  lines:
  - speaker: 1
    kind: 2
    text: "You hadn\u2019t even bothered to pay attention in class, just sat there
      to stew in your thoughts. Your eyes were trained onto the back of Bradley\u2019s
      head, trying to set him on fire with your eyes. He came into school again today,
      sporting a nasty bruise on his cheek. You couldn\u2019t help the fleeting feeling
      of gratification as you spotted it, until you realized that it made you sound
      almost like him, being happy that someone else is miserable as well. An unwell
      feeling settled into your gut, only lifting once the bell rang. "
    videoEventId: 
  - speaker: 1
    kind: 2
    text: 'Most students immediately leave for the cafeteria, talking amongst themselves.
      You stay rooted in your spot as Bradley walks over to you. He lifts one of
      his hands and pours the rest of his chocolate milk onto your desk. '
    videoEventId: 
  - speaker: 0
    kind: 0
    text: What, you got something to say?
    videoEventId: 
  - speaker: 1
    kind: 0
    text: You flinch at his snapping voice but realize that he is looking at another
      student a few desks over, daring him to say something to defend his classmate.
      The student just quickly shakes his head and flees.
    videoEventId: 
  - speaker: 0
    kind: 0
    text: "*snorts* That\u2019s what I thought. Fucking loser. "
    videoEventId: 
  - speaker: 1
    kind: 0
    text: 'With that he also leaves the room, most likely to look for Lacey and Lucas.
      Your hands are shaking from leftover adrenaline even minutes later. Once your
      heart has somewhat settled again, you finally stand up. '
    videoEventId: 
